abstract: >-
  An AI assistant's long-term memory, built week by week from one real mailbox, with every
  intermediate layer kept. The kaminski-v mailbox of the CMU Enron corpus (11,523 messages,
  November 1999 to February 2002) is replayed in arrival order into a file-based agent memory
  (eleman: markdown files in git). Each message is kept verbatim and turned into short notes by
  a model; once per week of mail an unattended consolidation distils the notes into the memory.
  The memory after each of the 122 consolidations is a git tag; every distilled fact links to its
  source message, and a ledger accounts for every message. All model work by Claude Opus 5.5.
